    "https://wd1.myworkdaysite.com/recruiting/scu/scu/job/Santa-Clara-CA/Assistant-Professor-in-Accounting_R7565": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor in Accounting",
      "description": "Assistant Professor in Accounting Skip to main content Sign In Search for Jobs Assistant Professor in Accounting page is loaded Assistant Professor in Accounting Apply locations Santa Clara, CA time type Full time posted on Posted 30+ Days Ago job requisition id R7565 Position Type: Assistant Professor in Accounting Position Type: Regular Salary Range: $182,580 - 202,867 Purpose: The Accounting Department in the Leavey School of Business at Santa Clara University invites applications for two full-time tenure-track faculty positions at the rank of Assistant Professor, beginning in Fall 2027. We encourage applications from candidates who will contribute to the diversity and excellence of our academic community, including individuals from historically underrepresented groups. Specialty or Sub-Discipline: Candidates in all areas of research and teaching interest are encouraged to apply. Qualifications: Ph.D. or ABD in accounting or closely related field by September 1 of the appointment year. Demonstrated capacity to undertake scholarly research publishable in leading academic journals. Commitment to contributing to Santa Clara University’s mission, including fostering a culture of inclusion and academic excellence. Responsibilities: Tenure-track faculty at Santa Clara University are teaching scholars expected to balance teaching, research, and service. This is an in-person position. Teaching Teach undergraduate and/or graduate courses in the faculty member’s area of expertise, as assigned by the department chair. High-quality teaching and significant faculty-student interaction are prioritized at SCU. The University provides extensive support for teaching development through its Faculty Development programs, which include workshops, grants, and mentoring opportunities. Teaching will be evaluated according to departmental standards and the principles of Ignatian pedagogy, which emphasizes respectful, inclusive, engaging, and evidence-based instruction. Research/Scholarly Work Maintain an active program of scholarly research publishable in leading academic journals. Each department maintains standards for scholarly work that contribute to the evaluation of tenure and promotion. The University strongly supports early-career faculty through mentoring and professional development resources. Service Provide effective service to the Department, School, University, profession, and/or community through committee work, leadership, professional engagement, and other contributions consistent with rank and experience. Application Procedure: Applications must be submitted through the University’s online application system, accessible via https://jobs.scu.edu/ Please include the following materials: Cover letter expressing interest in Santa Clara University and outlining qualifications. Curriculum vitae. Examples of research/scholarly work. Evidence of teaching effectiveness (both quantitative and qualitative, if available). Contact information for three letters of recommendation. Questions about this position may be directed to Matthew Cedergren, accounting@scu.edu Search Timeline: Review of applications will begin immediately and continue until qualified candidates are identified. Applications will be accepted until the position is filled. Please note that once application materials are submitted, applicants will no longer be able to access them through the online portal. About Us: Santa Clara University is a comprehensive, Jesuit Catholic university located in the heart of California’s Silicon Valley. Every student at SCU has the potential to do something extraordinary. The University offers more than 50 majors, minors, and special programs at the undergraduate level across the arts and sciences, business, and engineering, as well as graduate programs in business, engineering, education, counseling psychology, law, theology, and pastoral ministries. The Leavey School of Business is nationally recognized for its focus on innovation, entrepreneurship, strategy, and leadership. Among the first business schools accredited by the Association to Advance Collegiate Schools of Business (AACSB), the Leavey School consistently ranks highly in national rankings for both undergraduate and graduate business programs. Santa Clara University offers a comprehensive benefits package to eligible employees, including programs designed to support their personal health, well-being, and financial security, as well as that of their families. Telecommute Santa Clara University is registered to do business in the following states: California, Nevada, Oregon, Washington, and Illinois. Employees approved to telecommute are required to perform their work within one of these states. EEO Statement ​ Equal Opportunity/Notice of Nondiscrimination Santa Clara University is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants are encouraged to apply and will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, national origin, citizenship, ancestry, religion, age, sex, sexual orientation, gender, gender expression, gender identity, marital status, parental status, veteran or military status, physical or mental disability, medical conditions, pregnancy or related conditions, reproductive health decisionmaking, or any other characteristic protected by federal, state, or local laws.  For a complete copy of Santa Clara University’s equal opportunity and nondiscrimination policies, please visit the Office of Equal Opportunity and Title IX website at https://www.scu.edu/title-ix/ . Clery Notice of Availability Santa Clara University annually collects information about campus crimes and other reportable incidents in accordance with the federal Jeanne Clery Disclosure of Campus Security Policy and Campus Crime Statistics Act. To view the Santa Clara University report, please visit the Campus Safety Services website . To request a paper copy please call Campus Safety at (408) 554-4441. The report includes the type of crime, venue, and number of occurrences. Americans with Disabilities Act Consistent with its obligations under the law, Santa Clara University will provide reasonable accommodations to applicants and employees with disabilities.  Applicants who wish to request a reasonable accommodation for any part of the application or hiring process should contact the Department of Human Resources ADA Team at hraccommodations@scu.edu or by phone at (408)554-5750. Please note : This contact information is intended for accommodation requests only. Resumes or inquiries about application status sent to this inbox will not be reviewed or forwarded. For resumes or questions regarding application status, please contact hrservicedesk@scu.edu . Work Authorization: A foreign national who is appointed to a tenured or tenure-track faculty position is eligible for visa sponsorship assessment by Santa Clara University together with its legal counsel. Similar Jobs (14) Electrical and Computer Engineering Assistant Professor - Digital Systems locations Santa Clara, CA time type Full time posted on Posted 4 Days Ago Electrical and Computer Engineering Assistant Professor - Robotics & AI locations Santa Clara, CA time type Full time posted on Posted 4 Days Ago Assistant Professor in Animal Behavior or Behavioral Ecology locations Santa Clara, CA time type Full time posted on Posted 30+ Days Ago time left to apply End Date: October 2, 2026 (17 days left to apply) View All 14 Jobs About Us Santa Clara University is a comprehensive Jesuit, Catholic university located in California’s Silicon Valley, offering its 8,800 students rigorous undergraduate curricula in arts and sciences, business, and engineering, plus master’s, Ph.D., and law degrees. Santa Clara University does not sponsor work visas for staff positions. If hired, as a condition of employment with the University, individuals must provide verification of their identity and eligibility to work in the United States. Santa Clara University offers a comprehensive benefits package for benefit eligible employees with programs and resources designed to promote and sustain personal health care, well-being, and the financial objectives of our employees and families. Visit our benefits page for more information. Read More © 2026 Workday, Inc. All rights reserved."
